 ],
 "text": "Microsoft just told companies to treat AI agents like insider threats, and most setups I see make that worse. Here's the mistake. Someone connects an agent to email, the warehouse system, and the bank, all with 1 master key. Now, 1 bad instruction can touch everything. Satya Nadella said it plainly, separate the supply of intelligence from the authority over it. So here's how I build at Content Systems.ai. Each agent only sees what its job needs. It gets its own key. And a person approves anything that goes out. Emails, refunds, payments. In my live workshop, I build an AI employee with these exact rules with you. Want in, comment workshop, and I'll send you the details. The next date's in my profile."
